eral,  receive  calls  will  block until any (non‐zero) amount of
data is received, then return with  the  smaller  of  the  amount
available  or  the amount requested.  The default value for is 1.
If is set to a larger value, blocking receive calls normally wait
until they have received the smaller of the low‐water mark  value
or  the  requested  amount.   Receive calls may still return less
than the low‐water mark if an error occurs, a signal  is  caught,
